ollama (0.40.16+ds-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The source package is made the same every time from the same recipe:
    every file of debian/, the Lean toolkit prepare-lean.py copies in
    included, gets the recipe's date and modes before dpkg-source packs it
    (reproducible.py normalize-tree). The debian tarball of +ds-2 carried
    the toolkit's checkout times and the build's umask, so the exact rebuild
    of +ds-2 gave the same five archives byte for byte but another source
    package; +ds-2 is superseded by this version. No change in the programs.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:55:45 +0000

ollama (0.40.16+ds-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The service starts the engine on the card chosen for partners, and only
    on it (ORDER 70; the card is one choice shared by the Graphics and
    Partners pages): ExecStart goes through sparky-stereo-gpu-run --compute
    --category partners, which sets the variables that leave only that card
    visible to the CUDA, ROCm and Vulkan runners, or none for the processor.
    A card that cannot be used is said and kept, and the engine does not
    start. OLLAMA_IGPU_ENABLE=1, so a chosen integrated card is used.
    SyslogIdentifier=ollama keeps the engine's journal lines under its own
    name.
    Measured on an RTX 3060 and a Renoir APU with every runner installed:
    the RTX 3060 chosen runs on CUDA alone, the APU on Vulkan alone, the
    processor on the processor. Depends on sparky-stereo-graphics 0.2.16.
  * ollama-rocm-data's Lintian override names the four tags that fire for
    rocBLAS's GPU kernels (848 files each): the build of +ds-1 overrode
    arch-independent-package-contains-binary-or-object and showed the other
    three.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

ollama (0.40.16+ds-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ollama 0.40.16 (2026-11-09), upstream's release build for Linux amd64
    and its ROCm bundle, repackaged for Sparky Stereo OS (ORDER 70). The
    release publishes no signature for these files: each is checked by its
    pinned size and SHA-256, against the release's own sha256sum.txt (same
    origin as the files).
  * Split by hardware: ollama (the program, the processor and Vulkan
    runners), ollama-cuda (the CUDA 13 runner; NVIDIA's libraries come from
    NVIDIA's repository) and ollama-rocm (the ROCm 7.2 runner with AMD's
    libraries).
  * Left out of the repack, each with its reason in EXCLUDED.tsv: NVIDIA's
    CUDA libraries, the CUDA 12 runner, GCC's OpenMP library, and the copies
    of libdrm, libnuma and libelf that Debian ships.
  * The user service ollama.service listens on 127.0.0.1:11434 only and is
    not enabled at installation.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 03:18:00 +0000
